          },
          "worked": "Use $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$, $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}$ and $\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}$ with the completed triangles.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin30^\\circ&=\\frac12\\\\\\cos30^\\circ&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\\\tan30^\\circ&=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\\\\\sin60^\\circ&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\\\cos60^\\circ&=\\frac12\\\\\\tan60^\\circ&=\\sqrt3\\\\\\sin45^\\circ&=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\\\\\cos45^\\circ&=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\\\\\tan45^\\circ&=\\frac11=1.\\end{align*}$$",
